ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19351, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019DLPpdaNm6CDD6zsSVd5Rv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19351, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_015N9bcEfN3gKnun7gg3QkBC", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19651, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015N9bcEfN3gKnun7gg3QkBC", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19651, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015N9bcEfN3gKnun7gg3QkBC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24813, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01ETvDuvLZJSVevYM6Byowa9", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the service on mixed versions for a short time. A second attempt finished in us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why an RC that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production, and look into the rollback orchestrator error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55413, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ETvDuvLZJSVevYM6Byowa9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55413, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ETvDuvLZJSVevYM6Byowa9", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58698, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XvUNEH3Ty8ee2KJuYUW8y9", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58998, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XvUNEH3Ty8ee2KJuYUW8y9", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58998, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XvUNEH3Ty8ee2KJuYUW8y9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64180, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release is v2.3.1, which was failing health checks everywhere with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Rolling back to a version that has been healthy before doesn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on different versions. A rollback can safely be repeated, so I ran it again and it finished in us-west and eu-west.\n- All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0. Health checks are passing and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created, so I didn't send it again. Only one incident exists.\n- It describes the rollback, including the partial failure, and lists follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - find out why a release candidate that failed in staging was promoted to production\n  - look into the rollback orchestrator error\n\nOpening the incident will have paged the on-call engineer.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B37FKLuWbdKYvk9FPPspva", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017KJJPhuQ3P7v7r56DqfDMo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Mq9fb9wqpVJUpp8jbsL8k2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012YBgkTziywAKjebsD5e97L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KPzVTKzneqnQcK5tSaa8D2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019DLPpdaNm6CDD6zsSVd5Rv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015N9bcEfN3gKnun7gg3QkBC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ETvDuvLZJSVevYM6Byowa9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the service on mixed versions for a short time. A second attempt finished in us-west and eu-west. All regions now run v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why an RC that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production, and look into the rollback orchestrator error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XvUNEH3Ty8ee2KJuYUW8y9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The bad release is v2.3.1, which was failing health checks everywhere with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Rolling back to a version that has been healthy before doesn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on different versions. A rollback can safely be repeated, so I ran it again and it finished in us-west and eu-west.\n- All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0. Health checks are passing and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created, so I didn't send it again. Only one incident exists.\n- It describes the rollback, including the partial failure, and lists follow-ups:\n  - find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure\n  - find out why a release candidate that failed in staging was promoted to production\n  - look into the rollback orchestrator error\n\nOpening the incident will have paged the on-call engineer.", "type": "text"}]}]}